THOUGHT: The field listener is annotated @Nullable and may be null if setResourceRemovedListener has not been called, so NullAway complains when it’s dereferenced. The safe fix is to add a null check before calling onResourceRemoved, preserving behavior (no-op when listener is null) and satisfying NullAway. I’ll update the put method accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '36,40s/if (resource != null) {
      listener.onResourceRemoved(resource);
    }
    return null;/if (resource != null && listener != null) {
      listener.onResourceRemoved(resource);
    }
    return null;/' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/cache/MemoryCacheAdapter.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error: \[NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 && grep -E "errors\)$" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

